Your own attendance is separate from your students'. It appears as **My Attendance** in the drawer.

## How your attendance gets recorded

Usually by scanning your card, the same way students do — which is why the **RFID** field on your
teacher record matters. If it is empty, your scans go nowhere and your record will look like a run
of absences. Check it on [My Profile](/docs/educonnect-teacher-my-profile) and ask for it to be
filled in if it is blank.

Where an institute doesn't issue staff cards, attendance is recorded for you by the office instead.

## The monthly view

The monthly table lays out the month a day at a time. Read it for two things:

- **Days that are blank but shouldn't be** — you were in, but nothing was recorded.
- **The overall pattern**, which is what feeds the staff attendance figures an administrator sees on
  the Teachers dashboard.

## If a day is wrong

You cannot edit your own attendance — that is the point of it. Raise it with whoever handles staff
attendance at your institute, with the date. They correct it from **Teachers → Attendance**.

Do it promptly. A missing scan is easy to confirm the same week and much harder to reconstruct at
the end of the month.

